      "text": [
        "4201 - وَ قَالَ اَلصَّادِقُ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ : \"كُلُّ مَا كَانَ فِي اَلْبَحْرِ مِمَّا يُؤْكَلُ فِي اَلْبَرِّ مِثْلُهُ فَجَائِزٌ أَكْلُهُ وَ كُلُّ مَا كَانَ فِي اَلْبَحْرِ مِمَّا لاَ يَجُوزُ أَكْلُهُ فِي اَلْبَرِّ لَمْ يَجُزْ أَكْلُهُ\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.4201 - Imam Jafar ibn Muhammad Al-Sadiq (as), said:\n\"Everything in the sea that has a counterpart on land which is permissible to eat is also permissible to eat. And everything in the sea that does not have a permissible counterpart on land is not permissible to eat.\""
        ]
      }
    },
